# Phase 18 Lite request-header inheritance mapping

- Recorded: 2026-10-23 14:31:07 UTC
- Workspace: `/Users/bruce.tsai/Projects/trio/rocketmq-classic`
- Source revision: `5acaab89` (`fix(protocol): map Lite RPC request header inheritance`)
- Pinned Java source: RocketMQ 5.5.1,
  `efa1be59d6fc747ad220f036c86030f05f0419f9`

## Change

- The Java `LiteSubscriptionCtlRequestHeader` declares no payload fields and
  inherits `namespace`, `namespaced`, `brokerName`, and `oneway` from
  `RpcRequestHeader`. Rust previously used a unit struct and discarded those
  values.
- Rust now keeps the four fields private, exposes the inherited accessor
  surface, maps the four header keys, and compares/hashes only those fields.
  Java hash and `toString()` fixture values are checked in the Rust tests.
- The pinned identity/API fixture contains 46 entries and has SHA-256
  `421e054be509f5f56fb5f1fe0cd5870745c83e956f56831082858e9780b4a10d`.

## Verification

